      "style_a": "Brussels started enforcing the AI Act on Thursday, with the first compliance audits aimed at providers of general purpose models. Regulators said the opening round covers documentation, training data disclosure, and incident reporting. Firms that miss the filing window face fines of up to three percent of global turnover.",
      "style_b": "The AI Act was always going to arrive as paperwork rather than as a thunderclap, and here it is. What matters is not the fines, which are survivable, but the disclosure line, which forces labs to say out loud what they trained on. Expect the next six months to be an argument about definitions.",
      "status": "needs review"
